  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - RURAL ELECTRIFICATION DISTRIBUTION IMPROVEMENT AND FINANCING, through Government of Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This 404,510 technical Assistance (TA) activity supports the Rural Electrification Financing Corporation (REFC) to improve distribution systems and implement associated financing plans for rural electrification operations in the Philippines. With proper maintenance and loss control mechanisms in place, and procurement of equipment, materials and construction practices that meet international standards, distribution services are expected to significantly reduce losses on the grid-based system. Financing plans prepared for presentation to several identified financial participants will help REFC receive implementation financing approval. National Rural Electric Cooperative Association (NRECA) International has been identified as the sole-source contractor under a cost-sharing role for completion of the TA.</narrative>
  </description>
